<Project>

  <!--
    A static-analysis gate for the backend (NFR-MAINT-3), the same idea as the ESLint/Stylelint gate the frontend already has:
    applies to every project under src/ automatically (MSBuild walks up from each .csproj looking for this file).

    AnalysisModeSecurity=All turns every built-in security rule to at least a warning (SQL/LDAP/XML injection, weak crypto and
    hashing, insecure deserialization, certificate validation bypass, ...); the backend build step already treats warnings as
    visible and errors as build failures (see .github/workflows/ci.yml), so a new one is caught in CI, on the same pull request,
    without any extra wiring here.

    The rest of the analyzer catalog (performance, globalization, design suggestions like CA1848 or CA1305) is left at its
    default, much quieter severity: turning it on wholesale (AnalysisMode=Recommended) surfaces hundreds of pre-existing,
    stylistic findings across the codebase that are a separate cleanup, not a gate to add today.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <EnableNETAnalyzers>true</EnableNETAnalyzers>
    <AnalysisLevel>latest</AnalysisLevel>
    <AnalysisModeSecurity>All</AnalysisModeSecurity>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
